.TH AUTOWEBPNT 1 "July 2026" "autoWebPeNT 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
autowebpnt \- Automated Web Penetration Testing Framework
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B autowebpnt
[\-d \fIDOMAIN\fR] [\-\-cve \fICVE_ID\fR] [\-\-cve-file \fIFILE\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B autoWebPeNT
is an automated web penetration testing framework designed for Kali Linux. It orchestrates 15+ industry standard security tools across four sequential phases: Reconnaissance, Port Scanning, Web Enumeration, and Vulnerability Exploitation. It also includes a standalone CVE Valuation Engine to calculate financial risk and exploit probabilities. Output is generated as a client-ready executive PDF report (e.g., autowebpnt_report_example_com_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.pdf).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-domain\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR
Target domain to assess (e.g., example.com). Required unless \-\-cve or \-\-cve-file is used.
.TP
\fB\-\-cve\fR \fICVE_ID\fR
Evaluate single or comma-separated CVE IDs (e.g., CVE-2021-44228) and generate a financial risk valuation.
.TP
\fB\-\-cve\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
Evaluate a bulk list of CVE IDs from a text file (one CVE per line).
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-recon\fR
Skip Phase 1: Reconnaissance (Amass, Sublist3r, theHarvester, DNSRecon, WhatWeb).
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-scan\fR
Skip Phase 2: Port Scanning (RustScan, Nmap).
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-web\fR
Skip Phase 3: Web Enumeration (Gobuster, FFUF, Dirsearch, Nikto, WPScan, Nuclei).
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-exploit\fR
Skip Phase 4: Vulnerability Exploitation (Sqlmap, XSStrike, Commix, Hydra).
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fIN\fR
Maximum concurrent thread pool workers for parallel tool execution (default: 3).
.TP
\fB\-\-company\fR \fINAME\fR
Client or company name for report header (default: "Authorized Security Audit").
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-creds\fR
Show unredacted credentials in generated PDF report (default).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-creds\fR
Mask credentials in generated PDF report.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display CLI help banner and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. All requested phases completed cleanly.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid CLI arguments or usage.
.TP
.B 2
Pre-flight check failed. One or more required tool binaries were not found in PATH.
.TP
.B 3
Directory or environment initialization error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmap (1),
.BR amass (1),
.BR gobuster (1),
.BR nuclei (1),
.BR sqlmap (1)

